          "code": "MODIFYASSETFORM",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1774954113961",
          "id": "1774751610980",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1774751610990_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Objective:\nTitle: Confirm Changes for {{$context.$variables.SubscriptionProduct.ProductName}}\n\n## Summary (conditional):\n- If {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.actionPayload.ratePlanLabel}} exists and is non-empty,display EXACTLY this single sentence: You’re updating the rate plan to {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.actionPayload.ratePlanLabel}} for {{$context.$variables.SubscriptionProduct.ProductName}}.\n- If it does not exist or is empty, do not render any summary line.\n- Display the ratePlanLabel and ProductName in bold.\n- Validate and ensure that the summary line is displayed If {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.actionPayload.ratePlanLabel}} exists\n\n## Information Message (unconditional, must always render regardless of the summary)\n- Derive StartDateDisplay and EndDateDisplay as follows: \n• StartDateRaw = {{$context.$variables.SubscriptionProduct.StartDate}} \n• EndDateRaw = {{$context.$variables.SubscriptionProduct.EndDate}} \n• StartDateDisplay = the first match of regex [0-9]{4}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2} within StartDateRaw; if no match, use StartDateRaw as-is\n• EndDateDisplay = the first match of regex [0-9]{4}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2} within EndDateRaw; if no match, use EndDateRaw as-is\n- Render EXACTLY this line (no extra text, no field widgets): Select an effective date that is at least one day after today and on or before  <EndDateDisplay>. Ensure the quantity isn't negative.\n- Placement: directly below the optional summary and directly above the RecordWidget.\n- This is an informational message only. Do NOT render it as an input. Validate and ensure it is always displayed including the range that effective date can take.\n- Always display <StartDateDisplay> and <EndDateDisplay> in long date format such as MMM d, yyyy (e.g., Sep 1, 2025)\n\n## Required Fields Notice (must ALWAYS render; informational text only, not an input):\nRender EXACTLY this single line directly below the Information Message and above the RecordWidget: Review your updates, complete any required fields, and confirm to apply the changes.\n\n## Record Widget\nDescription: Display the summary, Information Message and Required Fields Notice in the description property. Display each of them in separate lines and add spacing between them.\nCreate an intuitive and user-friendly modify subscription input using a **RecordWidget** with the following properties. \nID: modifyAsset_confirmModifySubscription-$-{{$context.$variables.SubscriptionProduct.SubscriptionProductPuid}}_$_{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.actionPayload.ratePlanNumber}}. \nAlways use \"-$-\" as separator between \"confirmModifySubscription\" and SubscriptionProductPuid. Using this separator is essential to the working of the widget.\nAlways use \"_$\" as separator between \"SubscriptionProductPuid\" and ratePlanNumber. Using this separator is essential to the working of the widget.\nValidate that the id is as per specified above.\n\n\nThe form will include only the following input fields and a confirmation button, adhering to the following specifications:\n######Fields (only these four, in this order):\n###########\n1. Effective Date:\nAdd a date input field with:\nLabel: “Effective Date”\nID:  \"effectiveDate\"\n2. Change Reason\nAdd a select input field with \nLabel: \"Change Reason\"\nID: \"changeReason\"\noptions:  <options>\nvalue: <value>\nsubstitute <options> with {{$context.$nodes.EXTRACTCHANGEREASONS.$output.result}} \nsubstitute <value> with the first value from {{$context.$nodes.EXTRACTCHANGEREASONS.$output.result}} \n3.Comments\nAdd a comment inputText field with \nLabel: \"Comments\"\nID: \"comment\"\n4. Quantity\nAdd a quantity inputNumber field with\nLabel: \"Quantity\"\nvalue: {{$context.$variables.SubscriptionProduct.Quantity}},\nID: \"quantity\"\n\n####Validation\nThe Effective Date, Change Reason, Comments, Quantity fields are mandatory and should be validated before submitting the form.\nAlso Do not allow negative values for Quantity.\n############# Accessibility & UX:\n\nProperly label all form fields and logically group related inputs. Do not make the label all letters capital\nUse accessible markup and provide validation feedback to users.\nAdditional Notes:\n\n######Constraints\nDesign for clarity, ease of use, and accessibility best practices.\nOnly use the fields from the fields section\nPLEASE, maintain ID property as specified. It is very very IMPORTANT.\nDate formatting\n   - Always display dates in long date format such as MMM d, yyyy (e.g., Sep 1, 2025)\nCurrency formatting  \n   - Use currency symbol only (e.g., $ for USD) in all narrative amounts; do NOT append the code (avoid “$110 USD”).\nDo not display any other widgets, except for a **RecordWidget** to display the fields mentioned."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
